# Horosa Skill MCP Rules (thin — policy source of truth: `skills/horosa-agent/SKILL.md`)

- Any Horosa / 星阙 metaphysics output → call the Horosa MCP tools. Cursor gets the **compact surface** by
  default (13 facades + `horosa_tool_run`): call techniques by name via `horosa_tool_run(tool_name="qimen", …)`; the flat
  `horosa_cn_qimen` / `horosa_astro_chart` names only exist with `--surface full`, and the catalogue is the
  `horosa://catalog/techniques` resource. **Never hand-calculate** with Exec/Python/JS/web formulas — they
  bypass the runtime, Xingque defaults, export contract, memory, and reports.
- No `horosa` tools in the list? `horosa-skill setup --client cursor` (`uv run horosa-skill setup --client cursor`
  inside this checkout) registers everything; `horosa-skill doctor` is the health report.
- **Clarify before calling**: if a fact (time, place, gender, the moment of the question, target
  year) or a result-changing setting (house system, 起局方式, 贵人体系, 六爻 cast) is missing, ask a
  short question with options first — or call `horosa_agent_guidance`. Defaults only when the user
  explicitly accepts them (大六壬 default `guirengType: 2` 星占法贵人). Prefer `place` over lat/lon/zone.
- Gate protocol: tools refuse with `agent_guidance.required`; after the user answers the settings,
  include `agent_confirmed_settings: true` (`defaults_accepted: true` for accepted defaults)
  + `clarification_notes`. Facts go in the payload; no flag replaces them. With
  `details.agent_recovery.must_ask_user: true` → stop and ask with `prompt_to_user`; never
  self-confirm or switch tools to bypass.
- Trust only the returned `data.export_snapshot.export_text` (cut text: `warnings` give the follow-up call). Missing section →
  rerun `doctor` / `openclaw-check`; never claim MongoDB / port 7897 / Xingque Desktop / remote-DB
  dependencies.
- Full client policy + payload/report/troubleshooting sheets: `skills/horosa-agent/SKILL.md`
  (+ its `references/`). Repo/maintainer rules: `AGENTS.md`.
